id: ops-jarm
title: A binding created inside a conditional block is refused after the block because its child scope is popped
description: "The scanner pushes a child scope for a conditional block and pops that scope at fi, so every binding created only inside the block is invisible afterwards. This conservative refusal occurs even for one uniform block with no sibling arm; it is independent of the sibling-arm clear(). Preserving a binding after the block would require proving that every runtime path creates the same value without reopening the sibling-arm bypass."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: attestation,fail-closed,precision
created_at: "2026-09-01T06:56:23.826Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-01T07:10:01.355Z"
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: A future precision fix preserves a binding after a conditional only when the same value is proven on every runtime path; A binding created on fewer than all paths remains unproven and is refused; The sibling-arm bypass regression remains refused
risk: low
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T06:56:24.380Z",claude,"Reproduced against the canonical implementation at dd0121c:\n\njobs:\n  r:\n    steps:\n      - run: |\n          if [ \"$X\" = \"1\" ]; then FLAG=--provenance; else FLAG=--provenance; fi\n          npm publish $FLAG\n\nResult: failures=1, 'a publish invocation does not enable --provenance ... npm publish $FLAG'. FLAG is --provenance on every path, so the publish is attested and the refusal is a false positive.\n\nImpact is currently zero and the direction is safe. Running the canonical auditor against the real .github/workflows of all 22 fleet repositories gives OK for 21; the only non-OK is pm-rust, which correctly reports recognition=none because it is a Cargo crate that never runs npm publish and does not use this gate. No fleet workflow uses the identical-arms shape, so the convergence is not blocked by this.\n\nDeliberately not fixed in the same change as the bypass closure: joining arms is path-sensitive analysis, and loosening visibility is exactly the direction that reopens the sibling-arm bypass. It needs its own change with the bypass regression test still verified red on revert."
  "2026-09-01T07:10:01.355Z",pi-agent,"Uniform-block reproduction with no sibling arm: `if true; then FLAG=--provenance; fi` followed by `npm publish $FLAG` is refused. The child scope pushed for the conditional is popped at `fi`, making the binding invisible afterwards. This demonstrates that sibling-arm `clear()` is not the cause; it only enforces branch identity when a sibling exists."
body: ""
